+Add a local Pause/Resume movement control to the wardrobe. Freeze the currently delivered pose without changing the art node or starting another timer. A paused preview owns no RAF. Resume continues the original action for its remaining active duration. Keep the five movement controls and their Stop behavior. Stop, pose changes and live reduced motion cancel a paused run, with no replay when the preference returns. Manual pauses remain held while hidden; unpaused runs retain their existing absolute hidden-time expiry. Mirror and outfit updates stay usable while paused. No save or schema changes.
+
+Place a 48px icon button opposite Mirror in the stage's upper-left corner. It consumes no control row or character height. Use native disabled state before a movement starts, pause bars while active, a play triangle while paused, action-specific accessible labels and visible keyboard focus. Test all species and actions, repeated toggles, exact held art/grid/clock behavior, remaining lifetime, cancellation, hidden/resume behavior and live reduction. Review dressed paused species and the full layout/text matrix, with native painted-ink checks at both corners. Reject any overlap with visible art.
+
+The initial numerical red fails all 21 cases because the control is missing. The isolated candidate passes those 21 cases. The initial browser candidate passes 14 of 16 cases. Two fixture defects require correction before application: its geometry helper leaves an empty style attribute on active Bun Hop accents, changing serialized art despite zero paused RAF; and tilted Rest at 320px/200-percent text has a 60.5px² empty bounding-corner overlap with zero painted hits. Preserve the raw failures, full-art diagnostic JSON/PNG and fixture versions.
+
+The corrected geometry helper temporarily sets and restores the existing SVG pointer-events presentation attribute rather than adding an SVG inline style. It restores the button's exact original style attribute and uses native painted geometry for held movement layouts, while retaining strict nonoverlap for the initial static Head view. Both targeted cases pass. All 16 selected candidate PNGs were directly opened before product edits: 14 from the original run plus Bun and 320/200 from the corrected run. The original failed compact Rest and Bun Hop diagnostic PNGs were also inspected. Candidate product bytes stay unchanged through these fixture corrections.
+
+Native checks record delivered elapsed time instead of assuming the requested fake-clock phase was a rendered frame. Each of 45 movement runs holds its exact art for 60 simulated seconds with zero RAF, checks both facings and both corner controls, and resumes for the measured remaining duration. These give 180 sampled geometry views, not every instant or exhaustive pixel coverage. Native expiry is observed 24ms before and after the remaining deadline; numerical tests establish exact millisecond expiry. Root text enlargement is not browser zoom.
+
+The existing mirror regression contains the byte-identical faulty geometry function. Apply the same instrumentation correction there and add an immediate whole-art equality guard. Archive the original mirror fixture and verify its function bytes against the reproduced failing helper before the correction. This affects test instrumentation only; final native coverage includes all 18 existing mirror cases.
+
+Apply the exact isolated product candidate and run focused/full unit checks, production compilation, all 56 wardrobe browser cases, scoped lint and authored whitespace checks. Virtual candidate bundle builds do not typecheck; final production compilation is required. Use one sequential low-priority worker/browser with the existing RAM/tmp stop guard. Native Chromium and approximately one-second host resource snapshots do not certify other browsers, physical devices, human temporal comfort or peak CPU/RSS. No external publication.
